{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"01f4100c6dabf72cb5f905875be68734e4103afa79e76b1414237170742927db","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar_reconciler integration test fixtures","key_entities":["tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_roundtrip.py::_load_module","sys.modules[rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira.adf]","rich_text_codec.py::AdfCodec","AdfCodec.to_wire","test_cloud_functions_degrade_without_marklas","test_by_path_loader_preserves_module_identity_for_the_same_source"],"problem_keywords":["test isolation","module state leak","sys.modules replacement","test ordering","rich text codec","marklas state"],"propositions":["The integration fixture _load_module unconditionally replaces sys.modules with a fresh module B, but AdfCodec retains the prior module A, causing later tests to monkeypatch B while the codec still calls A","Serial test ordering with integration round-trip fixture followed by unit cutover test causes rich-text rendering mismatch when the codec binds stale module identity but the test fixtures install a different module object","The _load_module helper must cache modules by both canonical name and source path (__file__) to preserve module identity for the same source while allowing intentional replacement when source differs","Runtime identity instrumentation proved the codec follows the cached module A exclusively; monkeypatching the replacement module B had no effect on codec output"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787346737283312001,"uuid":"c95aff8c-95a9-41b7-b941-ac5c7bf2f2bb"}